# BUGS

A pass split by a draw that reads what the frame wrote loads its attachments again; a depth and stencil attachment of both planes can't be loaded on Mali.
An upload into a texture, a `glCopyTexImage2D` and a `glGenerateMipmap` end the open pass even when it doesn't read the image.
A clear with the colour mask partly off clears every channel; a partial stencil write mask clears all of the stencil.
`glCopyTexImage2D` into `GL_LUMINANCE` or `GL_ALPHA` keeps the framebuffer's other channels in the texture, which a shader reads.
A cube map's sampler is refused by vulkanlowering(2) (`a cube image`), so a program with a `samplerCube` doesn't link; nor does a program that samples a texture in its vertex stage.
A program given as SPIR-V draws into a window with the viewport flipped, so its `gl_FragCoord.y` counts from the window's top and `gl_PointCoord.y` is inverted there.
A buffer's attribute of another type than float is converted at every draw, not once.
`glDiscardFramebufferEXT` changes nothing that is stored.
The current context is the process's, not each thread's.
